-14|0@breakingbad^1440350857#cucyr8d:jpatton89$:RJ Mitte is one of the luckiest actors in all of Hollywood. He was on a powerhouse show, loaded with the best acting in television history. And here's RJ Mitte, who is mediocre at best when compared to his coworkers. He seems like a genuinely great guy, but the truth is...he only got the role because in real life he has a mild case of Cerebral Palsy. They could have gotten another actor who could have matched Bryan Cranston's energy...or Anna Gunn, Bob Odenkirk, Aaron Paul, Dean Norris, and Giancarlo Esposito's performances. But they didn't want to risk offending anyone by getting an able-bodied/good actor. So instead they went with RJ Mitte, who is now set for life. He will live off this one acting role for the rest of his life. He won the lottery. Good on him!
